From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: fence Ethernet DMA before teardown

Adapt the PR teardown contract to the current shared-GDM/QDMA driver,
without restoring the removed SOE buffers or offload stack. Allocate PPE
statistics through the NPU DMA domain and retain mappings until graceful
deinit or a verified terminal hardware fence.

Unregister netdevs before disabling NAPI. Terminal ndo_stop leaves mappings
intact; normal stop also retains them when DMA stays busy. Cover complete
RX/TX poll callbacks with RCU, drain their post-completion tails, mask and
free every requested shared QDMA IRQ, then reset hardware. Track partial
allocations and NAPI/IRQ registration for probe-failure unwind.

Release coherent rings, TX mappings and RX pages only when both PPE/NPU and
Ethernet DMA fences succeed. Gate direct NPU statistics MMIO after stop,
keep provider device links tied to consumer lifetime, and defer consumers
until PPE initialization is complete.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
